function web_faq():void{echo '<section class="section narrow"><p class="eyebrow">GOOD QUESTIONS, CLEAR ANSWERS</p><h2>Before you begin.</h2>';foreach(['Can I try it first?'=>'Yes. The login page offers connected fictional demo accounts. Real provider services are disabled in the shared sandbox. Please do not enter personal information there.','Who creates user accounts?'=>'Schools can invite and create users. Individuals can also request an account at a participating school; administrators verify roles and child links before access is granted.','How do plans and payments work?'=>'School registration shows the plans, billing cycles and trials configured by the platform. Paid activation requires server-verified payment. External providers may have their own charges.','Will it work on a phone?'=>'The interface adapts to smaller screens. Selected teacher tasks support offline capture; payments, provider services and synchronization require a connection.','Can we configure our school?'=>'Yes. Guided setup covers school identity, academic settings, people, finances and communication. The owner guide explains the operational modules and verification steps.'] as $q=>$a)echo '<details><summary>'.e($q).'</summary><p>'.e($a).'</p></details>';echo '</section>';}
function web_policy(string $page):void{web_title('CLEAR EXPECTATIONS',web_pages()[$page],'Effective 22 October 2026. Read this alongside your school’s notices and subscription agreement.');echo '<section class="section narrow prose">';$operator=af_setting('legal_name')?:'the platform operator identified in your subscription agreement';if($page==='privacy'){echo '<h2>Who handles information?</h2><p>Your school determines the purposes for processing its student, family and staff records. SchoolOS is operated by '.e($operator).'. Responsibilities, retention periods and provider arrangements must be recorded in the school’s applicable agreement and privacy notices.</p><h2>Information and purposes</h2><p>School accounts contain identity, school, academic, attendance, financial and communication records entered by authorized users. Registration collects names, email addresses and school details. Affiliate accounts additionally hold referral and payout details. Passwords are hashed; provider secrets are encrypted. Access is restricted by role, school and verified relationships.</p><h2>Children and lawful use</h2><p>Schools must establish a lawful basis under the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023, provide age-appropriate notices, verify guardian authority and obtain consent where required. Do not enter unnecessary sensitive information. AI and third-party messaging require school approval and suitable provider terms; do not submit children’s confidential information without authorization.</p><h2>Sharing, retention and your rights</h2><p>Configured payment, messaging, hosting and AI providers receive only the information required by the enabled workflow. Schools and the operator must document any international transfers and retention schedules. Ask your school administrator to verify and process requests for access, correction, restriction or deletion, subject to lawful record-retention duties. Unresolved privacy concerns may be raised with the Nigeria Data Protection Commission.</p><h2>Security and incidents</h2><p>Use individual accounts and report suspected unauthorized access promptly through your school administrator and support tickets. Operators must protect backups, encryption keys and server logs and follow their incident response and applicable notification duties. No software can guarantee absolute security.</p>';}elseif($page==='terms'){echo '<h2>Accounts and access</h2><p>Use SchoolOS only with authority from your school or the platform operator. Keep credentials private, provide accurate details and respect other users’ information. Schools approve membership and remain responsible for configured academic, financial and safeguarding decisions.</p><h2>Plans and payments</h2><p>Prices, billing cycles and permitted trials are displayed during registration. Paid service depends on verified subscription payment. This release does not automatically debit subscription renewals. Refund, tax and service-level terms follow your agreement with '.e($operator).'; contact the operator before purchasing if any term is unclear.</p><h2>Responsible use and availability</h2><p>Do not abuse messaging, upload unlawful material, probe other schools’ records or rely on AI as a substitute for professional judgement. Third-party services depend on configuration and provider availability. Schools must verify reports, reconcile payments and maintain recovery procedures.</p><h2>Affiliate participation</h2><p>Affiliate participation requires approval and acceptance of the program terms displayed at application. Commissions apply only to eligible verified subscription payments, subject to the recorded rate, holding period, reversals and withdrawal threshold. No earnings are guaranteed. Misleading claims, unsolicited spam and self-referrals are prohibited.</p>';}else{echo '<h2>Essential storage</h2><p>SchoolOS uses session cookies for authentication and form protection. A separate cookie selects the isolated demonstration environment. A referral cookie, when you follow an affiliate link, records a limited-duration referral token for attribution; it does not grant access to school records.</p><h2>Preferences and offline work</h2><p>Your browser may store theme choices, walkthrough progress and authorized offline teaching records. Synchronize outstanding work and clear locally stored records before handing over a shared device. Disabling essential cookies prevents sign-in. This website does not install advertising trackers.</p><h2>Referral choice</h2><p>Referral attribution lasts up to 30 days. You may clear it before registering a school.</p><a class="button" href="?page=cookies&clear_ref=1">Clear referral attribution</a>'; }echo '<p>Contact: '.e(af_setting('contact_email')?:'ask your school administrator to raise a platform privacy or support ticket.').'</p></section>';}
